       Q: Since maximising resource_efficiency has no upper bound, the optimiser will push throughput until a hard constraint is hit — meaning noise will settle at exactly 80 dB and fatigue at exactly 0.4 for the whole shift. Is that acceptable, or should the optimiser treat, say, fatigue ≤ 0.30 and noise ≤ 75 dB as preferred operating targets, with 0.4 / 80 dB as absolute ceilings only?
