  [Escalation] Remediation options presented to manager:
    - Option 1 — Add a Third Production Shift (Recommended): Introduce a third 8-hour shift to distribute the additional 20% demand load across more calendar time and more workers. By spreading the same workload across three shifts instead of two, per-shift machine utilisation and operator task density both fall, bringing the Fatigue Index well below 0.40 and reducing sustained noise exposure per worker below 80 dB. No constraint limits need to be changed. Requires authorisation to hire or redeploy shift staff and agreement with union/works council on shift rotation. Lead time to implement: 3–5 business days.
