      Preserves human constraints: Yes
    - Option 3 — Temporary Supervised Constraint Relaxation with Mandatory Mitigations (Last Resort): With explicit written approval from the EHS officer and production manager, temporarily raise the Fatigue Index ceiling to 0.57 and the Noise ceiling to 82 dB for a capped period of no more than 2 consecutive weeks. Mandatory mitigations must be in place before this option is activated: (a) mandatory 30-minute rest breaks every 90 minutes of high-intensity work, (b) provision and enforced use of EN-352 rated hearing protection (SNR ≥ 25 dB) for all workers on affected lines, (c) daily fatigue self-assessment check-ins logged in the CBPA system, and (d) automatic revert to original limits if any worker records a Fatigue Index event above 0.60 or noise dosimetry exceeds 85 dB(A) TWA. This option meets full demand but carries elevated occupational health risk and creates a regulatory compliance documentation obligation.
